## 📁 Project Structure

```
project_root/
├── config/                  # Project-level settings (replaces the default project name folder)
│   ├── settings/
│   │   ├── base.py          # Shared settings
│   │   ├── local.py         # Local dev overrides
│   │   └── production.py    # Production overrides
│   ├── urls.py
│   ├── wsgi.py
│   └── asgi.py
├── apps/                    # All Django apps live here
│   ├── core/                # Shared utilities, base models, mixins
│   ├── users/
│   └── <feature>/
├── static/
│   ├── css/
│   ├── js/
│   └── images/
├── templates/
│   ├── base.html
│   ├── components/          # Reusable partials
│   └── <app>/
├── media/
├── requirements/
│   ├── base.txt
│   ├── local.txt
│   └── production.txt
├── .env.example
├── manage.py
└── README.md
```

- Never put business logic directly in `urls.py` or `admin.py`
- Never use the default project folder name as a package; rename it to `config/`
- Keep each app focused on a single responsibility (SRP)
- Use `apps/` subdirectory to group all apps cleanly

