## ⚙️ Settings

- Always split settings into `base.py`, `local.py`, and `production.py`
- Never hardcode secrets — use `python-decouple` or `django-environ`
- Always set `SECRET_KEY`, `DEBUG`, `ALLOWED_HOSTS`, and `DATABASES` from environment variables
- Use `django-environ` or `python-decouple` for `.env` file management

```python
# config/settings/base.py
import environ

env = environ.Env()
environ.Env.read_env()

SECRET_KEY = env("SECRET_KEY")
DEBUG = env.bool("DEBUG", default=False)
ALLOWED_HOSTS = env.list("ALLOWED_HOSTS", default=[])
```

- Always define `AUTH_USER_MODEL` to a custom user model from the start
- Set `DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD = "django.db.models.BigAutoField"` in base settings

---

## 🗃️ Models

- Always use a custom user model (`AbstractUser` or `AbstractBaseUser`) — do this before the first migration
- Add `__str__` to every model
- Add `class Meta` with `verbose_name`, `verbose_name_plural`, and meaningful `ordering`
- Use `related_name` on all ForeignKey/ManyToMany fields
- Use `get_absolute_url()` for models that have detail pages
- Avoid `null=True` on string fields (`CharField`, `TextField`) — use `blank=True` with empty string default
- Use `blank=True, null=True` only on non-string fields where NULL is semantically meaningful

```python
class Article(models.Model):
    title = models.CharField(max_length=200)
    body = models.TextField(blank=True)
    author = models.ForeignKey(
        settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL,
        on_delete=models.CASCADE,
        related_name="articles",
    )
    created_at = models.DateTimeField(auto_now_add=True)
    updated_at = models.DateTimeField(auto_now=True)

    class Meta:
        verbose_name = "Article"
        verbose_name_plural = "Articles"
        ordering = ["-created_at"]

    def __str__(self):
        return self.title

    def get_absolute_url(self):
        return reverse("articles:detail", kwargs={"pk": self.pk})
```

- Use `TimeStampedModel` base class (via `django-model-utils`) or define your own
- Avoid logic in model `save()` — prefer signals or service functions for side effects
- Use database-level constraints (`unique_together`, `CheckConstraint`) where applicable
- Prefer `select_related()` and `prefetch_related()` in querysets, never in model methods

