## 🎨 Templates & UI

- Use a single `base.html` that all templates extend
- Use `{% block %}` tags for: `title`, `meta`, `content`, `extra_css`, `extra_js`
- Keep templates DRY — extract reusable elements into `templates/components/`
- Use `{% include %}` for partials; avoid duplicating markup
- Escape user input always — Django auto-escapes by default; never use `|safe` on user-generated content
- Use `{% url 'namespace:name' %}` — never hardcode URLs in templates

### UI Best Practices
- Use a CSS framework (Tailwind CSS preferred, or Bootstrap 5) consistently
- Use CSS custom properties (variables) for your color palette and spacing
- Keep all custom CSS in organized files — not inline styles
- Follow a mobile-first responsive design approach
- Use semantic HTML5 elements (`<main>`, `<nav>`, `<article>`, `<section>`, `<aside>`)
- Add `aria-*` attributes and `role` for accessibility (a11y)
- Always add `alt` text to images
- Use `<label>` properly linked to form inputs via `for`/`id`
- Flash messages: always display Django messages using the messages framework and style them clearly
- Loading states: show feedback for async actions (spinners, disabled buttons)

### Template Structure

```html
<!-- templates/base.html -->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{% block title %}My App{% endblock %}</title>
  {% block extra_css %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body>
  {% include "components/navbar.html" %}

  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    {% include "components/messages.html" %}
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
  </main>

  {% include "components/footer.html" %}
  {% block extra_js %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
```

