## 🚀 Performance

- Use `select_related()` for FK and OneToOne, `prefetch_related()` for ManyToMany and reverse FK
- Use `only()` or `defer()` to limit fields fetched from DB when appropriate
- Cache expensive querysets with `django.core.cache` or `django-redis`
- Use `django-debug-toolbar` in development to catch N+1 queries
- Add database indexes on fields used in `filter()`, `order_by()`, and `join` conditions
- Use `bulk_create()` and `bulk_update()` for batch operations
- Offload heavy tasks (emails, file processing) to Celery + Redis
- Use pagination for all list views — never return unbounded querysets to templates

```python
# Always paginate
class ArticleListView(ListView):
    model = Article
    paginate_by = 20
    template_name = "articles/list.html"
```

